Subject: Re: How to create the help files for self-defined funcs?
Message-ID: <200105021318.f42DIJE18566@arbres1a.FMR.Com>

Jingshan Zhang <jszhang at stat.rutgers.edu> wrote:
> where can I put together all my self-defined help files?

Brian Ripley <ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk> replied:
> See Chapter 8 of Venables & Ripley (2000)... (not covering 6.0 on Unix...)

Here's what I do in 6.0 on Unix.  Assume I want to document a function "myfunc"
in the library "Mylib", which lives under $S_LIB_LOC.
  1) At the S prompt, type > prompt(myfunc)
  2) Edit the resulting file myfunc.sgml, and place it in Mylib/HelpSrc/
  3) At the Unix prompt, type > update.help.pl Mylib

Here's my Perl script "update.help.pl":

#!/usr/local/bin/perl
# Update an S+ Help library
(($lib) = @ARGV) || die "Usage: $0 <libname>";
chdir "$ENV{S_LIB_LOC}/$lib/HelpSrc";
system("S HINSTALL ../.Data *.sgml .*.sgml");   # copies to __Shelp and __Hhelp
chdir "$ENV{S_LIB_LOC}/$lib";
system("S BUILD_JHELP Lib");                    # Creates __Jhelp

                                        -- David Brahm (brahm at alum.mit.edu)

