From peter_f_ellis at yahoo.com  Sat May  5 04:00:03 2001
From: peter_f_ellis at yahoo.com (Peter Ellis)
Date: Sat, 05 May 2001 12:00:03 +0800
Subject: subsets of explanatory variables in GLM
Message-ID: <006e01c0d517$fd2e2dc0$c3c43bcb@gsfisher>

All

A function that returns output like leaps but for a GLM is a simple task but
took me several hours to complete - so I post the attached function.  It
differs from leaps() in the following ways:

* allows factors as explanatory variables and will include/exclude the whole
factor (with whatever are your contrasts options) in different subsets

* allows non-Gaussian responses eg logistic regression (returns deviance and
AIC as measures of goodness of fit)

* returns an object of class leapsglm with convenient summary and plot
methods

For "normal" models:

* returns correct value of r2 and adjr2 for weighted data

* returns a value for the PRESS statistic

Its a bit slow, fairly clumsy, and people with large datasets are well
advised to make more efficient versions, but as far as I can tell it works.
It needs the V&R MASS library for the extractAIC function.  Please let me
know any comments, particularly bugs - my testing process has not been
completely rigorous.

cheers all
PE

Peter Ellis

leapsglm.SSC

Description: Binary data

