Professor Ripley has correctly pointed out to me that the use of "leaps" in
the name of the function and subsequent class referred to in my email below
was misleading, as fitting all subsets of explanatory variables for a GLM
really has nothing to do with the "leaps and bounds" algorithm.  I stand
corrected, and attach a revised version with more appropriate nomenclature
(the original name came out of my desire to produce *output* similar to that
of leaps, and was an error on my part).

cheers
PE

