Several responses were received to my question about
synchronizing Splus work files, laptop with desktop, on Win2000.

Several Linux/Unix fans hinted that I should lose Windows, and use the
"rsync"
utility. O, the temptation!
Win2000 synchronization problems appear to be breathtaking in number.
I've desynchronized the folders, & am resorting to a combination of 
MS SourceSafe for version control of function scripts, and Comparator, a
freeware folder-comparison program.  Some respondents mentioned 
alternatives to Comparator, including
Microsoft Briefcase (which I never liked) and Backer from Leanware, which is
got a shareware pricetag.

Several people concur that the mapping from object names to filenames
is at least part of the problem.  Restricting oneself to unmapped object
names ( 8+3 all lowercase) is mentioned as a solution.  I think it's too
restrictive and doesn't address all of the problem (bugs in MS
synchronization).

