From impromptu at nifty.com  Wed May  9 02:45:46 2001
From: impromptu at nifty.com
Date: Wed, 09 May 2001 11:45:46 +0900
Subject: summary: interpolation by ns()
Message-ID: <200105090245.AA00678@impromptu.nifty.com>

S-Plus users
E-mail: s-news at wubios.wustl.edu

Hi!
   I appreciate Dr. Thomas Yee's informative reply.
His WWW page below shows the detail of this problem
and countermeasures:

http://www.stat.auckland.ac.nz/~yee 

   And I learned that ns() and bs() in S-plus2000
have an argument to place boundary knots other than
the end points of data.

   A simple way for beginners is that the end points
for estimates are placed at the same points as those of data
even if the estimates at those points are not required.
This makes the position of knots unchanged when
estimates are derived by predict().

