From JimP at sonuspharma.com  Wed May  9 17:09:00 2001
From: JimP at sonuspharma.com (Jim Pratt)
Date: Wed, 09 May 2001 10:09:00 -0700
Subject: Use of get() to extract component within an object
Message-ID: <1BC608ACE9125D4588061A1A7E96A98C058180@sp-exch.sonuspharma.com>

Using S-Plus for Windows 4.5 & 2000.

I'm trying to extract components of objects, but am having difficulty.
I have several dataframes each with a response variable of interest.
The response variables are not the same name in the various dataframes,
nor in the same column number.  I'd like to perform similar code on each
response variable from the selected dataframes.  From the get() help
file:

You can not use get("a$b") to get the b component of object a; rather
this will attempt to get an object named "a$b". Use get("a")$b to get
the b component of a.

I can use get() to obtain the desired dataframe, but then having
difficulty extracting the desired component, and I've run into a brain
freeze.

core of code:

control<-data.frame(df=I(c('ph','ps','ps','pol','toc)),
        resp=I(c('PH','PARTMN','PART99','POLCONC','TOCOCONC')))

for(i in 1:13){
        df<-get(control$df[i])
        resp<-df$control$resp[i]
        }

If I can get resp within the for loop to be the response vector of
interest (e.g., ph$PH), then the rest of my script will go fine.  I'm
having trouble doing this. The code, as written, will try to assign resp
ph$"PH", which is clearly wrong. Please help.

Thanks,

Jim Pratt

Sonus Pharmaceuticals, Inc. 
jimp at sonuspharma.com 
(425)487-9500 x321 

From JimP at sonuspharma.com  Wed May  9 17:17:40 2001
From: JimP at sonuspharma.com (Jim Pratt)
Date: Wed, 09 May 2001 10:17:40 -0700
Subject: Re: Use of get() to extract component within an object
Message-ID: <1BC608ACE9125D4588061A1A7E96A98C0525F7@sp-exch.sonuspharma.com>

I found my answer.

Use resp<-df[[control$resp[i]]] to extract the component.

for(i in 1:13){
        df<-get(control$df[i])
        resp<-df[[control$resp[i]]]
        }

Sorry for taking up bandwidth.

Jim Pratt

