From pierre.duchesne at hec.ca  Fri May 11 01:09:12 2001
From: pierre.duchesne at hec.ca (pierre duchesne)
Date: Thu, 10 May 2001 21:09:12 -0400
Subject: Summary: multiplication of matrices in arrays
Message-ID: <3AFB3BB8.F53E6374@hec.ca>

Hello,

Thanks to Nick Ellis and Raphael Gottardo for their suggestions.
My original post is at the end.  Versions 1 and 2 are what
I tried.  Version 3 is the faster and is from Nick Ellis.

Thank you for your help,
Pierre Duchesne

set.seed(1)
A <- array( rnorm(3*3*200), dim=c(3,3,200) )
B <- array( rnorm(3*3*200), dim=c(3,3,200) )

# --- version 1 ---
now _ proc.time()
C1 <- array(0, dim=c(3,3,200) )
inverse.all <- array(apply(A, 3, solve), c(3, 3, 200))
for(i in 1:200) {
 C1[,,i] <- inverse.all[,,i] %*% B[,,i]
}
speed_ proc.time() - now
speed

# --- version 2 ---
now _ proc.time()
C2 <- array(0, dim=c(3,3,200) )
for(i in 1:200) {
 C2[,,i] <- solve(A[,,i],B[,,i])
}
speed_ proc.time() - now
speed

# --- version 3 ---
now _ proc.time()
C3 _ round(structure(apply(matrix(1:200,200,1),1,function(i,x,y)
     solve(x[,,i],y[,,i]),x=A,y=B),dim=c(3,3,200)),7)
speed_ proc.time() - now
speed

-------------
Original post:
-------------
