Hello,

Concerning my previous post, in the solution of Nick Ellis (version 3),
rounding
is not necessary in practice.  In fact I just cut and paste Nick's
solution, and
he told me that he did the rounding only to verify if the result in his
example was correct.

For the following two arrays:
set.seed(1)
A <- array( rnorm(3*3*200), dim=c(3,3,200) )
B <- array( rnorm(3*3*200), dim=c(3,3,200) )

the relevant code is then:
# --- version 3 ---
C3 _ structure(apply(matrix(1:200,200,1),1,function(i,x,y)
solve(x[,,i],y[,,i]),x=A,y=B),dim=c(3,3,200))

