Hello all,

this is not directly related to S.  I was wondering if anyone could suggest 
some good reading on the trade-offs between least squares and ML in 
structural or simultaneous equations.  I've seen claims that a least 
squares approach is less sensitive to specification error and to the 
presence of multicollinearity than maximum likelihood approaches 
(citations: Summers 1965; Cragg 1967)

Cragg, J.G. 1967. On the relative small-sample properties of several 
structural equation estimators. Econometrica. 35: 89-110.

Summers, R. 1965. A capital intensive approach to the small sample 
properties of various simultaneous equation estimators. Econometrica. 33: 1-41.

Does anyone have any later references, suggestions, refutations or opinions?

Thanks!

Andrew

