Thanks to Chuck Taylor, Steve McKinney, Jim Pratt and Nick Ellis for taking the
time to consider my question. Looks like there is no built in function for
calculating the (statistical) mode. For me, the best approach is probably
Steve McKinney's; he suggested

"Mode.default" <- function(x)
{
        tab <- table(x)
        as.numeric(names(tab)[which(tab == max(tab))])
}

"Mode.factor" <- function(x)
{
        tab <- table(x)
        names(tab)[which(tab == max(tab))]
}

"Mode.numeric" <- function(x)
{
        tab <- table(x)
        as.numeric(names(tab)[which(tab == max(tab))])
}

"Mode" <- function(x)
{
        if(is.category(x))
                Mode.factor(x)
        else UseMethod("Mode")
}

Of course, I still need to learn more about generic functions and/or methods
before this works for me. At the very least, it seems that I would need an
addition along the lines of:

"Mode.character" <- function(x)
{
        tab <- table(x)
        names(tab)[which(tab == max(tab))]
}

to deal with the case where x is character.

Thanks again to all concerned.

Dave Kane

