Antibiotic resistance of bacteria means that although antibiotics are in
the sample the bacteria keep growing. Non resitant bacteria stop growing or
will die. The concentration level of antibiotic in the sample is a measure
of the resistance level. When the basteria keep growing at a high
antibiotic concentration the laboratory stops finding out the exact level
(this is what I mean with truncated)

