From lbajuk at insightful.com  Thu May 17 21:24:02 2001
From: lbajuk at insightful.com (Louis Bajuk-Yorgan)
Date: Thu, 17 May 2001 14:24:02 -0700
Subject: Calling other programs
Message-ID: <008701c0df17$b29a9190$a66410ac@insightful.lan>

StatServer and S-PLUS provide a very flexible architecture for building
web-based applications. In a standard StatServer deployment
(IIS/ASP/COM/StatServer/S+) there would be a couple of different ways to
implement what you propose:

1) If the other program has a COM model, you could call it from the ASP page
or from within S+
2) If it can be called from the DOS command line, you could shell out from
within S+. Rather than waiting for a specified length of time, StatServer/S+
would wait until the
executable call returned, indicating the results were available.

However you do it, once the data file has been produced, StatServer could
grab it and include it in a web report.

