Subject: LOESS in S-Plus
Message-ID: <200105210408.AA00699@impromptu.nifty.com>

S-Plus users
E-mail: s-news at wubios.wustl.edu

Hi!

   The object below is the one I programed to make sure of the definition
of LOESS in S-Plus:

        span1 <- 0.5
        x0 <- 2.3       #  
##
        nd <- 20
        set.seed(110)
        xx <- seq(from = 1, length = nd, by = 0.1)
        xx <- xx^3
        yy <- cos(xx * 0.8) + rnorm(nd, mean = 0, sd = 0.3)     ##
##
        data1 <- data.frame(x1 = xx, y1 = yy)
        fit.lo <- loess(y1 ~ x1, data = data1, span = span1, family = 
"gaussian", degree = 1)
        data2 <- data.frame(x1 = x0)
        ey2 <- predict.loess(fit.lo, newdata = data2)
        print("LOESS in S-Plus")
        print(ey2)      ##
##
        kk <- as.integer(span1 * length(xx))
        dis <- ifelse(span1 < 1, sort(abs(xx - x0))[kk], span1 * sort(abs(xx - 
x0))
          [length(xx)])
        wt <- rep(0, length(xx))
        yes1 <- abs(xx - x0) <= dis
        wt[yes1] <- (1 - (abs(xx[yes1] - x0)/dis)^3)^3
        coef1 <- lsfit(xx, yy, wt)$coef
        ey3 <- coef1[1] + x0 * coef1[2] ##
##
        print("My LOESS")
        print(ey3)

The result is: 

[1] "LOESS in S-Plus"
[1] -0.1792257
[1] "My LOESS"
  Intercept 
 -0.1819646

   My understanding is that the "My LOESS" above is based on the standard 
definition
of LOESS. I would like to reproduce LOESS in S-Plus.

