Not quite.  It seems that it is equivalent to source-ing the code, and
source() is another alternative.  There can also be issues about where the
output goes, and submitting from a script window code that requires
interaction is an, erm, confusing experience.  (My class were doing
debugging that way on Monday.)

The issues are that both source() and submitting from a script back out all
the commits in the case of error, and so can use very much more memory in
the case of no errors.

