> without full backout capability, say by using a function...

In the mean time there is a way using Perl to trick S-PLUS into thinking
that you are submitting commands one at a time from the command line so
that it throws away the backout information and reuses the memory.  The
details are in the archive:
http://lib.stat.cmu.edu/s-news/Burst/15548

That's how I ran some pretty hairy simmulations for my dissertation
without having to copy/paste or babysit the computer while it ran them
overnight.

