>
> Having transferred these objects, then I open an object, e.g. graph1.aov,
> from Version 3.3. I got a message:
>
> Version 3.3 Release 1 for Sun SPARC, SunOS 5.3 : 1995
>
> > graph1.aov
> Error: Object "graph1.aov" not found
> In addition: Warning messages:
>   S-PLUS object(?) "graph1.aov" has unknown mode (0x2d010000) -- it does
> not
>         look like an S-PLUS object made on this machine
>
>
> While from Version 5, I receive a message:
> Version 5.1 Release 1 for Sun SPARC, SunOS 5.5 : 1999
>
> > graph1.aov
> function()
> logical(0)
>
>
>
> Does anybody know how to read this object from other versions?

The issue here is that the other version is a 64-bit version of S. If it
had been a 32-bit version, any post 4.0 version of S-PLUS would read
the objects.  (They automatically cope with big-endian vs little-endian,
and AFAIK all such platforms use the same IEEE formats for reals.)

The only really safe way I know is to find some kind soul with S-PLUS on a
Dec Alpha to run data.dump on your objects, and data.restore the dumps on
Solaris.

